  "full_text": "So, Portland's been judging the hell out of me. They're like, you need to get a job, eh? I'm like, no, I'm king. They're like, no, you need to get a job. So like, now it's my turn. I'm like, you know what my job is? It's like judging the city. Like, I gotta go around, say, wham. Anyway, so my job is judging the city. So, you know what? Judge not lest you be judged, right? So, like, isn't that the truth, though? Like, who's vile? Think of some vile people. The really judgmental ones are almost always... The more judgmental... A judgmental person is usually, by definition, vile. You know what I'm saying? Like, you ever seen a judgmental person that's not vile? I'm just saying. Like, the really judgmental people, those are the most vile. Judge not lest you be judged. So, wow. That's an interesting insight. Wow",
